  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/filopaludina-siamopaludina-martensi-cambodjensis/",
      "html": "<p>A typical viviparid snail that shares all the characters of the family. Filopaludina (Siamopaludina) martensi cambodjensis attains a length of about 4 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/filopaludina-siamopaludina-martensi-cambodjensis/",
      "html": "<p>They are no algae-eaters in the strict sense, but feed on Aufwuchs and detritus. Food tablets (produced for ornamental fish) are a reliable food for them in the aquarium.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/filopaludina-siamopaludina-martensi-cambodjensis/",
      "html": "<p>There are males and females; the males can be recognized by the fact that one of the antennas is modified in shape.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/filopaludina-siamopaludina-martensi-cambodjensis/",
      "html": "<p>These snails are livebearers.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/filopaludina-siamopaludina-martensi-cambodjensis/",
      "html": "<p>These animals breathe via gills, not via lungs, and thus use the dissolved oxygen in the water for breathing, like fish do. For the first time ever this snail was imported from Thailand.</p>"
    }
  ],
